          "answer": "probably_no",
          "justification": "Clinical monitoring and recorded death dates measure all-cause mortality directly, without cause attribution or disability grading. This is a suitable and sensitive method for detecting survival differences in the reported window. Missing follow-up is separately appraised in D3; the approved window discrepancy does not make death ascertainment intrinsically invalid.",
