          "question_id": "sq:selection:prespecified-analysis",
          "answer": "probably_yes",
          "justification": "The applicable 05TB SAP version 2.0 dated April 5, 2015 explicitly describes itself as final prior to unblinding and covers this comparison, all randomized ITT adults, overall survival over the operational nine-month follow-up, and treatment-only Cox regression stratified by HIV and MRC. These specifications correspond to the reported primary HR. The original/final protocol named stratified log-rank; the SAP explicitly explains the change to Cox as essentially equivalent while adding HR and CI. Thus correspondence is to the final SAP, not an assertion that the original protocol was identical. Main-report masking until last follow-up and confidential independent DSMC access support probable pre-unblinding finalization.",
          "unknowns": [
            "Actual investigator/statistician unblinded outcome access dates and database-lock audit are not supplied.",
            "Operational randomization-date equivalence and broader nine-month window remain the approved scope uncertainties."
